(II.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 688 Tm
(Consider the physical book: its weight in the hand, the faint) Tj T*
(scent of paper and binding, the small geography of a dog-eared) Tj T*
(corner. These are not incidental pleasures. They are the body of) Tj T*
(reading, and the body matters. To resume a book is to return to) Tj T*
(a place one has been, and the worn page is a kind of map.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 587.5 Tm
(But the digital page, too, has its quiet virtues. It remembers.) Tj T*
(It carries an entire shelf in a single slim pane of glass and) Tj T*
(asks nothing of the dusty corner. The trick, if there is one, is) Tj T*
(to make the new vessel as hospitable as the old; to give the) Tj T*
(wandering eye a margin to rest in, and the returning reader the) Tj T*
(exact line where he left off.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 468.5 Tm
(For there is no small cruelty in losing ones place. The reader) Tj T*
(who must hunt for the sentence he abandoned the night before) Tj T*
(loses not only time but the thread of feeling, the warmth that) Tj T*
(the page had gathered. A readers tool should hold that warmth) Tj T*
(as carefully as a hand cupped around a candle.) Tj T*
ET

endstream
