(III.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 688 Tm
(And so we come to the modest argument of this essay: that the) Tj T*
(manner of reading is not indifferent to the matter. A noisy room) Tj T*
(spoils a tender chapter. A cluttered page exhausts the eye. The) Tj T*
(reader deserves a room of his own, even if that room is only a) Tj T*
(rectangle of warm light on a screen, framed in the calm of) Tj T*
(unhurried type.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 569 Tm
(Let the margins be generous. Let the type be honest and old, the) Tj T*
(kind that has set ten thousand pages before this one. Let the) Tj T*
(page fill the width of attention and nothing more. And when the) Tj T*
(reader rises and goes about his day, let the book wait exactly) Tj T*
(where he left it, the ribbon still tucked between the pages.) Tj T*
/F1 12.5 Tf
18.5 TL
1 0 0 1 84 468.5 Tm
(This is all that reading asks of us, and all that we, in turn,) Tj T*
(might ask of the things we read upon: a little quiet, a little) Tj T*
(warmth, and the patience to be returned to.) Tj T*
1 0 0 1 84 375 Tm
